        "id": "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27",
        "title": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "2b040f66-f01d-5bd7-8cc9-fb81c65ab3c6",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=e^{\\frac{1}{t}},\\,y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{2} + 1}},\\,0<t<\\infty,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=- \\frac{e^{\\frac{1}{t}}}{t^{2}},\\,y'(t)=- \\frac{t}{\\left(t^{2} + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\left(- \\frac{t}{\\left(t^{2} + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\right)}{\\left(- \\frac{e^{\\frac{1}{t}}}{t^{2}}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{t^{3} e^{- \\frac{1}{t}}}{\\left(t^{2} + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=2,$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t=2} & =\\frac{\\left(2\\right)^{3} e^{- \\frac{1}{\\left(2\\right)}}}{\\left(\\left(2\\right)^{2} + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5 \\sqrt{5} e^{\\frac{1}{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8 \\sqrt{5}}{25 e^{\\frac{1}{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
